The proposed solution will provide an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents' work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities. This tool will facilitate access to reliable and up-to-date information, assist with drafting administrative contents, and provide accompaniment in the instruction of files. The solution will also suggest actions or steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process.

To ensure successful project coordination and governance, we will leverage our experience in managing complex projects and adopt a phased methodology, such as PRINCE2 or Agile Scrum. A steering committee will oversee the project's progress, meeting monthly to review progress, discuss challenges, and make strategic decisions. We will also maintain a RAID log and decision log to track risks, assumptions, issues, and decisions throughout the project.

Our technical architecture will utilize large language models (LLMs) such as Mistral 7B, LLaMA 3, CamemBERT, and Falcon, as well as retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) frameworks like LangChain, LlamaIndex, and Haystack. We will employ API gateways like Kong or Apigee to facilitate secure and standardized interactions between the AI solution and various business software, civil status, town planning, electronic document management (EDM) systems, and user directories.

To ensure high availability and performance, we will implement monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, or ELK stack to track system health and optimize response times. Our target is to achieve a time of response lower than 2 seconds for current requests, with a high level of relevance of the answers. We will also guarantee an availability of 99.9%, compatible with the needs of the municipal services.

In terms of security and compliance, we will ensure that our solution complies with the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR) and hosts data exclusively within the European Union. No transfer of data outside the EU will be authorized, and sensitive data will be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). We have a Data Protection Officer appointed and contactable at dpo@nexus-engineering.it, and our standard data residency policy ensures that all data is stored within the EU only.

Our approach to change management and training of agents will include assigning a dedicated change manager responsible for developing and delivering targeted training programs. These programs will include in-person workshops and e-learning modules tailored to the needs of the municipal agents, ensuring they are comfortable using the new AI solution.

We will also prioritize digital sobriety practices, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation to reduce GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching for an estimated 20% recompute reduction, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle. Our carbon reporting capability, based on the GRI Standards (partial), will help monitor and report the solution's environmental impact.

The proposed solution will be hosted on a SecNumCloud-type infrastructure or equivalent, within the European Union, to comply with GDPR requirements. We have experience working with green hosting partners like OVHcloud and Scaleway, which use 100% renewable energy and are located in France.

Our budget proposal is based on a phased approach, aligning with the client's requirement for progressive deployment. Given our standard daily rates and pricing model, we can allocate resources efficiently across the four-year period. Our target gross margin percentage is 28%, and we have a minimum acceptable margin of 18%. We will provide a detailed breakdown of costs across each year, considering both the development phase and the subsequent maintenance and support phases.

We believe that our proposal meets all the requirements and constraints outlined in the call for tenders, including the technical, functional, and regulatory aspects. Our solution will improve the efficiency of the City of Belval's administrative services and the quality of service rendered to users, while ensuring compliance with GDPR and other relevant regulations. We are confident that our expertise and experience make us an ideal partner for this project, and we look forward to the opportunity to work with the City of Belval.
